{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dino Explore has 4 gamemodes: </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Digsite</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2D indie style gamemode where you're located in a digsite.....</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The point of this gamemode is to find facts and dig up dinosaur bones. There comes waves of ores that you can mine. With the ores, you can buy facts and trade them for special items. These special items can allow you to have a higher chance of finding bones or allowing you to mine a certain ore.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Find Dinosaurs</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This gamemode unlocks &quot;Comparison Room&quot; and &quot;Question Room&quot;. (meaning you must complete this gamemode to get access to those gamemodes)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Find Dinosaurs is exactly what it sounds like. You're supposed to find dinosaurs. You move around in 2D world and look for dinosaurs. When you have found a dinosaur, you can learn some facts about it. There are a total of 28 dinosaurs and you need to find all of them to complete this gamemode.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When a dinosaur is found , you can find it in &quot;Library&quot;. Library is where you can reset the whole game (all gamemodes) and see what dinosaurs you have left to find</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Question Room</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a dinosaur quiz game. You have 55 different questions, and most of them , depending on how much you know about dinosaurs are challenging. This gamemode are for those who want to challenge themself and learn about dinosaurs. Everytime you answer correctly, you gain 1 answer point. Everytime you answer wrongly, you lose one point (unless you're at 0). When you have gotten a certain amount of points, dinosaurs and terrain will show up on your screen. You can tap on these objects and they will make a sound!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Comparison Room</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This gamemode is all about comparing. Compare dinosaurs with a man, woman, hyena, house and a truck. Both dinosaurs and compare objects are of realistic size.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is for people that want to know how big dinosaurs truly are. Some might be smaller than you expected and some might be bigger than you expected!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3788740?t=1756227723","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3788740?t=1756227723","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3788740/9969df12041faa68f65e1c9a802ffde79d269a42/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1756227723","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3788740/9969df12041faa68f65e1c9a802ffde79d269a42/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1756227723","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dino Explore has 4 gamemodes: </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Digsite</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2D indie style gamemode where you're located in a digsite.....</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The point of this gamemode is to find facts and dig up dinosaur bones. There comes waves of ores that you can mine. With the ores, you can buy facts and trade them for special items. These special items can allow you to have a higher chance of finding bones or allowing you to mine a certain ore.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Find Dinosaurs</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This gamemode unlocks &quot;Comparison Room&quot; and &quot;Question Room&quot;. (meaning you must complete this gamemode to get access to those gamemodes)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Find Dinosaurs is exactly what it sounds like. You're supposed to find dinosaurs. You move around in 2D world and look for dinosaurs. When you have found a dinosaur, you can learn some facts about it. There are a total of 28 dinosaurs and you need to find all of them to complete this gamemode.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When a dinosaur is found , you can find it in &quot;Library&quot;. Library is where you can reset the whole game (all gamemodes) and see what dinosaurs you have left to find</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Question Room</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a dinosaur quiz game. You have 55 different questions, and most of them , depending on how much you know about dinosaurs are challenging. This gamemode are for those who want to challenge themself and learn about dinosaurs. Everytime you answer correctly, you gain 1 answer point. Everytime you answer wrongly, you lose one point (unless you're at 0). When you have gotten a certain amount of points, dinosaurs and terrain will show up on your screen. You can tap on these objects and they will make a sound!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Comparison Room</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This gamemode is all about comparing. Compare dinosaurs with a man, woman, hyena, house and a truck. Both dinosaurs and compare objects are of realistic size.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is for people that want to know how big dinosaurs truly are. Some might be smaller than you expected and some might be bigger than you expected!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","developers":["Simon Nordl\u00f6w"],"genres":[{"description":"RPG","id":"3"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3788740/46cf799901909515da5312e0fd70237d4f99ba1d/header.jpg?t=1756227723","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"highlight":tr